Enable the MTP drafter's vocab-truncated draft head (40960 tokens) for
Qwen3.5 / Qwen3.8-27B W4A16-AutoRound checkpoints on XPU.

Companion to qwen35-embed-quant.patch; apply it AFTER the embed patch.
Without this patch the MTP drafter loads the full ~248k-row lm_head
(7.2x the memory of the 40960-row draft head) even though the
checkpoint only ships mtp.draft_lm_head.* for 40960 rows, so the
draft head silently stays unpopulated and speculative decoding is
degraded (draft quality ~ random over the full vocab).

What it does:
- Qwen3_5MultiTokenPredictor.__init__: if the checkpoint directory
  contains mtp_draft_vocab_ids.pt (built by syvai's
  build_draft_vocab.py), construct a 40960-row ParallelLMHead as
  model.draft_lm_head and map checkpoint mtp.draft_lm_head.* weights
  onto it in load_weights(). Set MTP_DRAFT_VOCAB=0 to disable.
- compute_logits(): scores the 40960-row head, scatters logits back
  to the full vocab (-inf for non-draft ids). Speculative decoding
  stays exact: the target model still verifies full-vocab candidates,
  only the drafter's proposal distribution changes.

Apply from the installed vllm package directory:
  patch -p1 -d venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/vllm < qwen35-mtp-draft-vocab.patch
or from a vllm checkout (vllm/ package dir):
  cd vllm && git apply ../qwen35-mtp-draft-vocab.patch

Validated: git apply --check clean on upstream vllm main (29af8bd,
2026-07-30) and on Suppressor72/vllm fix/mamba-retention-eagle-boundary
(74a6570), in both cases applied after qwen35-embed-quant.patch.

